[Music]  i'm kean kaplan  as a neuroscientist living with  tourette's ocd and adhd  i study what makes my brain different  from the average person  growing up i struggled academically and  socially  paying attention sitting still and  waiting my turn were everyday challenges  in the classroom and i was definitely  bullied a lot  it wasn't until i was 14 when i watched  a documentary about tourette's and  realized  holy i have that  my life changed the moment i was  diagnosed by a neurologist  the doctors gave me a word for what i  was experiencing but they still couldn't  explain why it was happening or how to  make it stop  why can't i control the movements and  sounds i make why aren't there better  treatments for people like me  these are the questions that inspired me  to pursue a career in neuroscience  yes it's been hard but nobody  understands the experiences and  challenges of brain disorders better  than the people living with them we need  neurodiverse people to study the brain  because our perspectives are critical to  scientific progress both in the lab and  society

